# S Core — The Complete Heart

S is one product, one symbol, one command.

## What is "complete" for a developer opening S today

1. One command: `s`
2. One source extension: `.s`
3. One project file: `project.se`
4. One lockfile: `s.lock`
5. One docs family: `.sd`
6. Errors that speak human S, not Python
7. New project in one step that runs immediately
8. Test, check, run, symbols — all offline

## Core engine layout

  s          → CLI (the face)
  src/       → Core engine (lexer → parser → checker → interpreter | SVM)
  src/slib/  → Standard library (.s modules)
  hub/       → Packages
  studio/    → Editor brain (LSP)
  examples/  → Joy, not confusion

## Promise

Every `s run` path should either succeed clearly or fail with an S-shaped error.
No half-story: if a feature is listed, it must work offline without external accounts.
